  "preconditions": [
    "Owned complete current project artifacts and review records; Core review diagnostics, no effective profile or authentication claim.",
    "Native complete model, independently evaluated verification input and exactly one bound native code-state observation per code_ref."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Query all direct incoming/outgoing neighbours and Appendix J review observations; compare independent groups/reasons/identities and guard currentness and all read-only boundaries.",
    "Compare literal domain facts and explicit absence, preserve affected/review sets across order and cache changes, and reject stale or invalid source data without writes or inferred verification.",
    "Compare one immutable computed observation across validation, impact, trace, diff, coverage and built-in verification/traceability views; refuse foreign, incomplete or untyped inputs without subject writes.",
    "Recompute saved complete currentness inputs from a bound native Work snapshot; compare single and resumed coverage/code/verification data and reject changed model, product, scope, time, trust or code bindings before producing a result."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "`impact`, `diff`, `traceability`, `coverage` und `release readiness` MÜSSEN unreviewed, suspect und invalid Relations getrennt ausweisen und deren betroffene Artefakte erklären.",
    "scope": "12.t.W/R supply opt-in native currentness across validation, impact, trace, diff, coverage and built-in views. Versioned inert Work inputs bind the complete Evaluation, time, scope, project configuration, every original record (including historical/unselected Evidence), and every native code observation. Resume recomputes and refuses changed or missing bindings; separate native Waiver trust is rechecked. Scoped model views retain the full inventory without widening their evaluation. Whole-inventory consumers refuse partial scopes. Incremental query work retains all verification/currentness inputs beyond pagination. Fresh Core/PYZ processes restore all necessary bytes from a trusted native CheckpointStore at a new location; no original source locator is needed. No Subject writes, external execution or Release Readiness claim. QueryWork remains a process-local cursor, not a serialized executable continuation."
  },
